================================================================================
VENDORED CODE
================================================================================

`smoke_covenant/_vendor/` carries code and extracted logic from the same
author's `smoke-suite` monorepo (`trust/smoke_trust/`), under the same
Apache-2.0 licence. Same author, same licence, no third-party origin —
recorded here because a reader of the file alone cannot tell that.

- `asn1.py` and `rfc3161.py` — exact copies of
  `trust/smoke_trust/audit/asn1.py` and `trust/smoke_trust/audit/rfc3161.py`.
  Byte-identity with the originals is asserted by SHA-256 in
  `test_vendor_conformance.py`; do not edit these files or that check fails.

- `primitives.py` — canonical-JSON and `smoke-merkle-v0` logic (canonical
  JSON encoding, Merkle root/proof/verify) extracted from
  `trust/smoke_trust/iea/contract.py` and
  `trust/smoke_trust/attestation/windowed.py`. Reproduced as standalone
  functions rather than copied wholesale because the originals live inside
  larger modules with unrelated dependencies; byte-for-byte behavioural
  agreement with the originals is asserted by randomized differential
  testing in `test_vendor_conformance.py`.

- `signer.py` and `tsa.py` — standalone equivalents of `smoke_trust`'s
  `SoftwareMeasurementSigner` and `smoke_trust.audit.anchor.TSAClient`,
  respectively: mechanically identical in behaviour (same signing scheme,
  same RFC 3161 client defaults) but written independently for this package
  so it does not hard-depend on a `smoke-suite` checkout. Not byte-for-byte
  copies and not covered by the conformance check above. `signer.py` carries
  two classes: `LocalKeySigner`, which requires a caller-supplied key and is
  the standalone equivalent used for real signing, and `DemoSigner`, which
  mints an ephemeral key and is for demos and tests only.

