THE COMFYUI BOUNDARY
================================================================================

ComfyUI (https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI) is licensed GPL-3.0.
This project vendors, patches, forks, or redistributes none of it.
`smoke_covenant/adapters/comfy.py` and `comfy_node/` are runtime hooks: they
import ComfyUI's public extension points (`folder_paths`,
`comfy.sd1_clip.load_embed`, the `CacheProvider` registration point) at
execution time, inside ComfyUI's own process, entirely at call time or load
time within that process. No ComfyUI source is contained in, copied into, or
modified by this repository. This is the established ComfyUI custom-node
pattern and is conventionally treated as a separate work rather than a
derivative one — see the module docstrings in `smoke_covenant/adapters/comfy.py`
and `comfy_node/__init__.py` for the specific choke points hooked and the
reasoning. That factual basis — no vendored or modified ComfyUI code, only a
runtime import of its public extension points — is why this project's own
code is licensed Apache-2.0 here. No general conclusion about GPL-3.0/
Apache-2.0 compatibility is asserted beyond that.
